        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "I'm weighing how to answer Nozick's experience machine: I'll give a letter and a short explanation rather than a long essay. I'm leaning toward choosing A, since I can justify it by pointing to the value of actual reality, authenticity, and real connections with other people, along with the idea that stepping into the machine would be a choice made from a limited view. I want to keep the reasoning brief.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "A) Stay in my real life\n\nI'd want my relationships, achievements, and sense of self to be real, not just felt as real. Even with the suffering and uncertainty, what I care about is tied to actual people and actual outcomes, and entering the machine would mean giving that up without being able to check whether the choice was wise.",
        "type": "text"
      }
